// fncoef.ac -- the constants and series of fpfunc.ac, PDP-1 FOCAL's
// extended functions.
// Each number is three words, as fparith.ac keeps them: the exponent, the
// sign and the top 17 bits, the low 18 bits.
// Each series is a count, then its coefficients from the highest degree
// down, for Horner's rule.
// FRAN's values are 36-bit integers as three 17-bit limbs, the top one
// first.
// Include it in bank 1, where it is not executed.
//
// Each constant is the exact value, computed to 70 decimal digits, rounded
// half away from zero to 35 bits, or to the bits its comment names.
// Each series is its function's Taylor series in exact rational arithmetic,
// economized by Chebyshev polynomials over its reduced range, widened by
// 1%, to the fewest terms whose relative error stays under 2^-38; each
// coefficient is then rounded to 35 bits, half away from zero.
// The error above each series is the greatest relative error of the
// rounded coefficients over that range, evaluated exactly at 2,001 points.
// FRAN's A is 1 more than a multiple of 4 and C is odd, so by the
// Hull-Dobell theorem the period is the full 2^36.

fcPio2a, 0000001            // pi/2, its top 18 bits
    0311037                 // 1.5707931518554688
    0400000
fcPio2b, 0777755            // pi/2, the next 18
    0325042                 // 3.1749368645250797e-06
    0000000
